      "why": "pipelined_m also gives 1 result/cycle (meets throughput) but registers every m stages, cutting FF count and area/power at the cost of a longer combinational path (lower Fmax) and higher latency. This is the key power-vs-Fmax trade-off family: for a battery design, a modest m may drop power_index below full pipelining while still clearing 50 MSPS. m capped at 4 to keep Fmax high enough for the throughput constraint."
