  "rationale": "The hard constraint is throughput_msps >= 50, which forces 1 result/cycle (pipelined or pipelined_m) or a very high-Fmax unrolled_k. iterative is excluded because its 1-result-per-(N+3)-cycles throughput cannot plausibly reach 50 MSPS. The accuracy constraint max_abs_err <= 2^-12 is met by the accuracy-determining parameters (data_width, n_iter, angle_guard, frac_guard, rounding), which are identical across families, so I bound them to the 2^-12-feasible band (data_width 14-20, n_iter 12-20) to focus budget on the real trade-off: power_index vs accuracy_bits. The objective is min power_index with accuracy as the trade-off, and the selection rule is min power_index, so the front is dominated by the power axis; pipelined (best Fmax/latency) and pipelined_m (FF/power reduction) carry the most budget, with unrolled_k as a smaller probe for a potentially lower-power feasible point. Rounding is kept as a 2-choice factor since it shifts accuracy at no structural cost."
